<title>SPAIN: Spain's Rato says economy not overheating.</title>
<headline>Spain's Rato says economy not overheating.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish Economy Minister Rodrigo Rato said on Tuesday that the economy was not overheating and that inflation would be at about two percent at the end of the year.</p>
<p>&quot;I don't think we are seeing a phenomenon of overheating of the economy,&quot; Rato told the parliamentary group of the Popular Party.  </p>
<p>Rato said Spain's monetary policy had contributed &quot;very efficiently&quot; to a reduction in inflation.</p>
<p>&quot;We can assume that 1997 inflation will end around two percent,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The government recently revised its year-end inflation forecast to 2.2 percent from 2.6 percent.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2161</p>
